Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["PoincareDualityAlgebra", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"9fc9379a-0b75-43fc-a7d8-c12754176dd5"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["PoincareDualityAlgebra"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/PoincareDualityAlgebra", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["complex", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "79ae210d-176d-4608-9b0a-980247daad66"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the finite-dimensional Poincar\[EAcute] duality algebra of a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CochainComplexWithPairing"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CochainComplexWithPairing", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0ab0ba32-2487-47e8-8135-117afc2f818d"],
 " that carries a product and has a perfect pairing.",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"2e7f30d8-45ac-4710-9d9a-265d3d6eb147"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["PoincareDualityAlgebra"]], 
     "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/PoincareDualityAlgebra", 
     "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["data", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ba5d9ab1-73d3-44b5-80f3-8db3ec7d8959"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is a finite-dimensional Poincar\[EAcute] duality algebra given by an \
Association ",
 StyleBox["data", "TI"],
 " of its basis, degrees, Gram matrix, differential and triple products, the \
object ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["NondegenerateQuotient"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/NondegenerateQuotient", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9d315b34-9746-47af-8085-be2805394bf7"],
 " gives."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"2b64dccb-8088-42d7-92bc-9a6f1214cd66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is a tagged object, read with ",
 StyleBox["algebra", "TI"],
 "[",
 StyleBox["key", "TI"],
 "] and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Normal"]], "paclet:ref/Normal"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "19c1c6a6-6435-4e65-b129-709ee5387d00"],
 ". For a basis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "1"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["N", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"54fa5057-5166-47f8-9ee8-db88075d5d34"],
 " of degrees ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}]},
    "Abs"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0a397c38-6ae8-4c65-8683-9cd28cfab46e"],
 " and the pairing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
    RowBox[{"-", ",", "-"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"68e9807f-6ca5-4948-aa65-6ebe40d07254"],
 " of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "003000ad-5214-44b1-987b-17c5bebb2896"],
 " it has the following keys:"
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the algebra is the object the \
AlgebraicModels part hands to the ChernSimons part: GradedPairing[algebra] \
reads the alphabet off it, and CanonicalMaurerCartan reads the canonical \
element off its triple product, so the dependency runs one way (R5c). It is \
built from data by PoincareDualityAlgebra[complex], from a \
CochainComplexWithPairing with a product, and not by a new constructor from \
degrees, Gram matrix and product, which an earlier report proposed: the \
four-argument CochainComplexWithPairing already takes that data and validates \
it, and the conversion is the inverse of CochainComplexWithPairing[algebra], \
so no new data shape enters the API (R3, kept by Pavel). A pairing that is \
not perfect gives a Failure, and a complex without a product returns \
unevaluated, since it has no triple product. The usage message sits beside \
the constructor from a complex since R5b. Prior art: the Wolfram Language has \
no Poincare duality algebras. T17 pins the two conversions as inverse to each \
other, and the algebra of the quotient of the complex of a model as the \
quotient of the model, on the fourteen catalogue models; the quotient itself \
is pinned against the engine of the verification suites.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
